    icon: '💡',
  },
  data: {
    LLM: "Play tiles that create double headers or triple headers for immediate points. Prioritise playing doubles to set up a triple header.\n\nSuit counting: each pip value appears on 8 tile-ends in a double-6 set. Once a double is played, half that suit's ends are taken up. Use this to predict whether a double header will hold or be broken. Hold doubles as long as possible to convert a double header into a triple header.\n\nBlocking strategy: if you realise you cannot score easily, aim to block the game by managing which suits are available at the ends. A blocked game awards 2 points to the lightest hand — sometimes deliberately constrain the ends to force a block when you hold fewer tiles than opponents. Track what opponents have drawn (if any) to infer their tile composition.",
    Player: "Play tiles that create double headers or triple headers for immediate points. Prioritise playing doubles to set up a triple header.\n\nSuit counting: each pip value appears on 8 tile-ends in a double-6 set. Once a double is played, half that suit's ends are taken up. Use this to predict whether a double header will hold or be broken. Hold doubles as long as possible to convert a double header into a triple header.\n\nBlocking strategy: if you realise you cannot score easily, aim to block the game by managing which suits are available at the ends. A blocked game awards 2 points to the lightest hand — sometimes deliberately constrain the ends to force a block when you hold fewer tiles than opponents. Track what opponents have drawn (if any) to infer their tile composition.",
    aggressiveness: 0.5,
    riskTolerance: 0.5,
    bluffFrequency: 0.3,
    bluffSettings: {
      profile: 'balanced',
    },
    basic: 'Play tiles that create double headers or triple headers for immediate points. Prioritise playing doubles to set up a triple header.',
    intermediate: "Suit counting: each pip value appears on 8 tile-ends in a double-6 set. Once a double is played, half that suit's ends are taken up. Use this to predict whether a double header will hold or be broken. Hold doubles as long as possible to convert a double header into a triple header.",
    advanced: 'Blocking strategy: if you realise you cannot score easily, aim to block the game by managing which suits are available at the ends. A blocked game awards 2 points to the lightest hand — sometimes deliberately constrain the ends to force a block when you hold fewer tiles than opponents. Track what opponents have drawn (if any) to infer their tile composition.',
    tips: [
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: 'Doubles are the most powerful tiles — they are both required for triple headers and hard to play offensively by opponents.',
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: 'Target the same pip value at both ends as soon as possible; a triple header (3 pts) beats two separate double headers (4 pts total) only if you can sustain it.',
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: 'In a blocked game, the player with the fewest tiles scores 2 pts — factor this into late-game play when your hand is light.',
      },
    ],
  },
